        {
          "block_label": "text",
          "block_content": "Taiwan’s National Health Insurance (NHI) program, which began in 1995, is a mandatory universal health insurance program that covers more than 99% of the Taiwanese population. $ ^{10} $ The NHIRD is managed by the National Health Research Institutes (NHRI) of Taiwan and consists of detailed healthcare data from more than 28 million enrollees. It includes coverage for outpatient, inpatient, emergency, dental, and traditional Chinese medicine services. The Longitudinal Health Insurance Database is a subset of the NHIRD and is a representative database containing 1,000,000 patients randomly",
